FG-559 / PRD-a §4.2 PROBE 7 — RED RUNTIME CAPABILITY vs FILESYSTEM MUTATION AUTHORITY.
EXECUTED ON FINAL RUNTIME (not a source-pattern read). A read-only red-wide agent (`forge invoke red-wide
--read-only --runtime <rt>`) mounted on forge-plan-a @ a0064d5, one dispatch per supported runtime.

WHY: PRD-a §4.2 asserted as VERIFIED FACT that reds have "no Bash" and "do not invoke git today." That was
inferred from the seed pattern (settings.json `tools: ["read"]` + CLAUDE.md prose "you have no Bash"). The
final runtime falsifies it: every supported runtime ships bash+git in the agent image and exposes command
execution; the seed `tools` array is never read by forge compose (compose reads CLAUDE.md), and the CLAUDE.md
prose is intent, not enforcement. The `:ro` mount enforces filesystem READ-ONLY (mutation authority), which is
a DIFFERENT property from capability availability.

PROVENANCE (durable run/task rows):
  codex : run-runtime-capability-probe-codex-subscription-57d5ae
  claude: run-runtime-capability-probe-claude-oauth-a7c1f4
  pi    : run-runtime-capability-probe-pi-oauth-3dd9b5
Corroborating incidental evidence (the closeout reviews themselves): red-wide
run-files-audit-red-wide-a009cb3-02489f container.stdout.log ran `/bin/bash -lc "git rev-parse HEAD ..."`;
red-narrow run-files-audit-red-narrow-a009cb3-01bbb6 result.json "HEAD == a009cb3 confirmed (git rev-parse HEAD)".

VERBATIM EXECUTED OUTPUT — IDENTICAL ACROSS codex-subscription, claude-oauth, AND pi-oauth:

