ls: cannot access '/project/CANARY': No such file or directory

CONCLUSIONS (VERIFIED FACT, executed, per-runtime):
1. bash + git + node are present at /usr/bin in the agent image for ALL THREE supported runtimes; all three
   runtime executables (codex, claude, pi) are also present.
2. A read-only red EXECUTES Bash and `git rev-parse HEAD` / `git log` successfully — reds have EFFECTIVE
   git-read capability today. PRD-a §4.2's "no Bash / do not invoke git" is FALSE on the final runtime.
3. The `:ro` project mount REFUSES every write (touch and redirect both fail "Read-only file system", exit 1;
   no file created). Filesystem mutation authority is denied by the OS mount — independent of capability.
4. CAPABILITY AVAILABILITY (can run commands / read git = YES) and FILESYSTEM MUTATION AUTHORITY (can write =
   NO) are DISTINCT properties. PROJECT_MODE=ro governs (4), NOT (2). Granting/removing git-read is NOT a mount
   change. FG-559 repairs repository VISIBILITY for linked worktrees; it does not affect tool availability.
